WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.732 --> 00:00:17.995
One day the children were walking by the fence along the top of the hill, beside the railway

2
00:00:18.035 --> 00:00:23.659
line. The ground was very rocky, but some grass and small trees grew.

3
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.701
The children were looking for wild cherries.

4
00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:29.884
Suddenly they heard a noise.

5
00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:35.130
The noise was soft but very clear, and slowly it began to get louder.

6
00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.511
"Look at the tree over there!"

7
00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.491
shouted Peter.

8
00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:42.913
The girls looked and saw a tree moving slowly down the hill.

9
00:00:44.074 --> 00:00:45.934
The tree was moving toward the railway line!

10
00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:50.236
"It's magic!"

11
00:00:50.657 --> 00:00:51.217
said Phyllis.

12
00:00:52.497 --> 00:00:54.578
"I knew the railway was magic!

13
00:00:55.679 --> 00:00:58.320
Look, some other trees are moving too!"

14
00:00:59.604 --> 00:01:04.346
It really did seem like magic—all the trees seemed to be walking down the hillside!

15
00:01:05.606 --> 00:01:07.907
A loud rumbling sound filled the air.

16
00:01:07.927 --> 00:01:11.488
"Oh, I don't like it!

17
00:01:12.488 --> 00:01:13.448
Let's go home!"

18
00:01:13.908 --> 00:01:14.549
said Phyllis.

19
00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:19.230
But they all watched as the trees slipped slowly down the hillside.

20
00:01:21.271 --> 00:01:25.932
Then some stones and loose earth fell down and rattled on the railway tracks far below.

21
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:29.086
A big rock began to move too.

22
00:01:29.106 --> 00:01:35.950
"It's all coming down," Peter tried to say, but he was too scared to speak.

23
00:01:37.612 --> 00:01:42.895
More rocks, grass, trees, and bushes slipped off the hill and crashed onto the tracks below.

24
00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:45.997
A cloud of dust rose up.

25
00:01:46.017 --> 00:01:48.559
"It's blocked the tracks!"

26
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:49.640
cried Phyllis.

27
00:01:53.923 --> 00:01:55.004
said Peter, thinking.

28
00:01:56.212 --> 00:01:58.774
"And the 11:29 hasn't gone past yet.

29
00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:04.577
We must let them know at the station, or there will be a terrible accident," Bobbie said.

30
00:02:04.597 --> 00:02:06.978
"There isn't time!"

31
00:02:07.378 --> 00:02:07.979
said Phyllis.

32
00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.201
"It's after eleven now," Peter said.

33
00:02:13.402 --> 00:02:14.402
They thought for a moment.

34
00:02:14.422 --> 00:02:18.945
"We need something red to get people's attention," said Peter.

35
00:02:18.965 --> 00:02:22.086
"Then we could go down and wave to the train."

36
00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.568
They started to walk down the hill.

37
00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:29.575
Bobbie was pale, and Phyllis was red-faced and worried.

38
00:02:29.595 --> 00:02:33.418
"Oh, how hot I am!"

39
00:02:33.818 --> 00:02:34.278
she said.

40
00:02:34.298 --> 00:02:37.441
"I thought it was going to be cold.

41
00:02:38.562 --> 00:02:43.025
I wish we hadn't put on our She stopped suddenly and looked excited.

42
00:02:43.045 --> 00:02:46.208
"Our petticoats!"

43
00:02:46.648 --> 00:02:47.349
Phyllis cried.

44
00:02:47.369 --> 00:02:49.110
"They're red!

45
00:02:50.031 --> 00:02:51.092
Let's take them off!"

46
00:02:52.224 --> 00:02:56.747
The girls took off their petticoats, and the three children ran to the sharp bend in the railway

47
00:02:56.787 --> 00:02:59.529
line. The train would be coming soon.

48
00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.973
"Now," said Peter, taking hold of the largest flannel petticoat.

49
00:03:05.994 --> 00:03:08.415
"You're not you're not going to tear them?"

50
00:03:08.816 --> 00:03:09.476
asked Phyllis.

51
00:03:09.496 --> 00:03:15.881
"Phyllis, if we can't stop the train, there'll be a real accident, with people killed!"

52
00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:16.761
Bobbie said.

53
00:03:18.142 --> 00:03:20.504
Peter divided each petticoat into three pieces.

54
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.121
Then he looked at his watch again.

55
00:03:23.141 --> 00:03:25.462
"We've got seven minutes.

56
00:03:26.523 --> 00:03:27.944
We'll need some sticks as well."

57
00:03:29.064 --> 00:03:31.606
They found some sticks and tied the flannel onto them.

58
00:03:32.966 --> 00:03:34.607
Now they had six red flags.

59
00:03:35.688 --> 00:03:40.250
The children made two little piles of rocks on the tracks, and stuck a red flag in each.

60
00:03:41.451 --> 00:03:43.492
Then Phyllis and Bobbie each took a flag.

61
00:03:43.512 --> 00:03:48.655
"I will have two flags because I'm the one who tore them," said Peter.

62
00:03:50.764 --> 00:03:53.768
"They're our petticoats though," Phyllis began to argue.

63
00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:55.651
But Bobbie interrupted.

64
00:03:56.633 --> 00:03:57.314
"Who cares?

65
00:03:57.995 --> 00:03:59.457
We have to save the train!"

66
00:04:00.358 --> 00:04:03.683
Perhaps Peter's watch was slow, or perhaps the train was late.

67
00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:06.507
They seemed to wait for a long time.
